---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Generic header</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body-l">A generic header to help services not on GOV.UK</p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Example</h2>
  <div class="govuk-generic-header">
    <div class="govuk-generic-header__container govuk-width-container">
      <div class="govuk-generic-header__logo">
        <a href="/" class="govuk-generic-header__homepage-link">
          My cool service
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:START (auto-generated - edited content will be overwritten by scripts/update-component-guidance.mjs) -->
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the Generic header component if your service is both:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>a public-facing government service</li>
    <li>
      not on the GOV.UK website (meaning that your service is not part of the <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/govuk-proposition/govuk-proposition"
        >GOV.UK proposition</a
      >)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    This is to bring consistency and maintain user trust in journeys that move
    between the GOV.UK website and other government websites and services.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    This component also helps ensure your non-GOV.UK service does not:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>identify itself as being part of GOV.UK</li>
    <li>use the crown or GOV.UK logotype in the header</li>
    <li>use the GDS Transport typeface</li>
    <li>
      use the <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://brand.design-system.service.gov.uk/colour/govuk-blue/"
        >GOV.UK brand colours</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    See the guidance on <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://www.gov.uk/service-manual/design/making-your-service-look-like-govuk"
      >if your service is not on GOV.UK in the Service manual</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When not to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    If your service is hosted on one of these gov.uk domains, you must use the <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/header/"
      >GOV.UK header component</a
    > instead:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>gov.uk/[myservice]</li>
    <li>[myservice].service.gov.uk</li>
    <li>[myblog].blog.gov.uk</li>
  </ul>
  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:END -->
</Layout>
